1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,360
Utopia: where can you find it? Nowhere. Just desert, a few buildings, and things

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,121
under the sand.

3
00:00:05,341 --> 00:00:07,091
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,291
Shuffle the twelve Sand Snake cards to make the Sand Snake deck.

5
00:00:11,291 --> 00:00:12,721
That's all the extra setup.

6
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:15,768
Each turn the Sand Snakes rise up and attack.

7
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:19,443
At the end of the Killer phase, draw two Sand Snake cards and follow them.

8
00:00:19,663 --> 00:00:23,457
Each snake does one damage to one target in the named space, in this order:

9
00:00:23,457 --> 00:00:26,340
a Victim first, then you, then a Minion, then the Killer.

10
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,396
For example, this one attacks the Crossroads, or the Bunker if the Crossroads has

11
00:00:30,396 --> 00:00:30,869
collapsed.

12
00:00:31,089 --> 00:00:32,860
Then they burrow back underground.

13
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:37,614
Sand Snakes aren't Minions. You can't attack, kill or otherwise deal with them,

14
00:00:37,614 --> 00:00:41,411
except that Reaction cards and Item effects can prevent their damage to you.

15
00:00:41,631 --> 00:00:44,823
One card tells you to reshuffle the discard pile into the deck.

16
00:00:44,823 --> 00:00:48,116
Do that after resolving any other Sand Snake cards drawn with it.

17
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:53,254
Boulder spaces, with this icon, are safe from Sand Snake attacks, and some cards

18
00:00:53,254 --> 00:00:54,011
refer to them.

19
00:00:54,231 --> 00:00:56,784
Some ranged weapons reach further from a Boulder:

20
00:00:56,784 --> 00:01:00,119
the Six-Shooter gets range two, and the Scoped Rifle range four.

21
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:03,530
Some Terror and Event cards make a space collapse.

22
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:07,789
Earthquake!, for example: roll a die, one to three the Crossroads, four to six the

23
00:01:07,789 --> 00:01:08,464
Trailer Park.

24
00:01:08,684 --> 00:01:11,387
When a space collapses, every Victim in it is killed.

25
00:01:11,387 --> 00:01:15,468
You and any Enemies there take damage, and anyone left panics until they're out.

26
00:01:15,688 --> 00:01:19,800
Put a Sinkhole token there. Nobody can move into or through that space for the rest

27
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,683
of the game. There are four Sinkholes.

28
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,873
Dehydration resets your Time to five at the end of each Planning phase, unless you

29
00:01:26,873 --> 00:01:29,113
have some left over. The Canteen cures it.

30
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:32,986
Stalkers makes you draw three Sand Snakes each turn instead of two.

31
00:01:32,986 --> 00:01:35,221
Landslide! closes the Mountain Pass exit.

32
00:01:35,441 --> 00:01:37,644
The Bulldozer Keys let you drive the Bulldozer:

33
00:01:37,644 --> 00:01:41,159
while you're with it, you and Victims in your space ignore the Sand Snakes.

34
00:01:41,967 --> 00:01:45,868
A few tips. Treat the Sand Snakes as a second Killer and check which spaces they

35
00:01:45,868 --> 00:01:46,063
hit.

36
00:01:46,283 --> 00:01:49,781
Fight from the Boulders, where you're safe and ranged weapons reach further.

37
00:01:50,001 --> 00:01:53,318
And Sinkholes are permanent, so keep your route to the exits open.

38
00:01:53,318 --> 00:01:53,820
Good luck.

